---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About - Glade Francis"
  description="Glade Francis is a software developer in Salt Lake City and the founder of Struxr."
>
  <section class="px-4 md:px-6 lg:px-6 pt-20 pb-20 lg:pt-36 max-w-2xl">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[var(--color-text-muted)] text-base leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        I'm Glade Francis. I've been building software and web applications in Salt Lake City since 2007. I run a software development shop called Struxr.
      </p>
      <p>
        For most of my career, my core work was client websites, SEO, and small web applications. Building a full-scale software product from scratch required a team and months of runway. Pairing nearly twenty years of software architecture with modern AI tooling changed that math—now I can design, test, and run much larger software systems myself while still doing the web and search work I've done for decades.
      </p>
      <p>
        There's a popular take right now that SaaS is dead. I don't buy it. Big, one-size-fits-all SaaS is what's dying. For years, small businesses got pushed into the "nobody ever got fired for buying Salesforce" trap—sitting through endless demos with sales reps and paying thousands a month for bloated platforms where they only touch ten percent of the features.
      </p>
      <p>
        SaaS didn't die; it moved down a level. Now it makes sense to build sharp, niche software for specific trades, or to take a solid product and customize it directly around how a specific ten-person company operates.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's how <a href="/projects/cpa-relay" class="text-[var(--color-text)]">CPA Relay</a> started. My wife runs a CPA firm, and every practice management tool on the market got in her way during tax season. She walked me through the pain points and I built CPA Relay to her specs. I also run <a href="/projects/paypolka" class="text-[var(--color-text)]">PayPolka</a> for service business billing and <a href="/projects/krux-crm" class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Krux CRM</a> for small teams.
      </p>
      <p>
        The website and SEO world is in just as much flux. AI has made it easy for anyone to spin up a passable website in an afternoon, and AI assistants are changing how people search. Honestly, that's great—nobody should pay an agency ten thousand dollars for a basic brochure site anymore. But when generating code and copy gets cheap, judgment becomes the bottleneck. Knowing how to migrate a domain without tanking ten years of search traffic, structuring clean static HTML that Google and AI crawlers actually read, and turning a messy business into clear pages that convert still takes experience.
      </p>
      <p>
        When I take on outside client work—whether that's building or redesigning a website, handling SEO, customizing one of my existing products, or replacing a tangle of spreadsheets with a custom web app—you work directly with someone who has been doing this since 2007 and knows where the landmines are buried.
      </p>
      <p>
        I occasionally post on X as <a href="https://x.com/tiller_ing" rel="me noopener" target="_blank" class="text-[var(--color-text)]">@tiller_ing</a>. If you want to talk, <a href="/contact" class="text-[var(--color-text)]">send me a note</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
